{"metadata":{"publication_info":[{"year":2018,"page_end":"206","page_start":"1","journal_issue":"1","journal_title":"Acta Math.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214886"},"journal_volume":"220"},{"year":2018,"page_end":"206","page_start":"1","journal_issue":"1","journal_title":"Acta Mat.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214888"},"journal_volume":"220"},{"material":"publication","pubinfo_freetext":"Acta Mathematica, 220:1-206, 2018"}],"citation_count":208,"citation_count_without_self_citations":179,"dois":[{"value":"10.4310/ACTA.2018.v220.n1.a1","source":"FIZ Karlsruhe"},{"value":"10.4310/acta.2018.v220.n1.a1","source":"International Press"},{"value":"10.4310/acta.2018.v220.n1.a1","source":"arXiv","material":"publication"}],"urls":[{"value":"https://www.quantamagazine.org/to-test-einsteins-equations-poke-a-black-hole-20180308/","description":"Quanta Magazine article"}],"titles":[{"title":"The global non-linear stability of the Kerr-de Sitter family of black holes.","source":"FIZ Karlsruhe"},{"title":"The global non-linear stability of the Kerr–de Sitter family of black holes","source":"International Press"},{"title":"The global non-linear stability of the Kerr-de Sitter family of black holes","source":"arXiv"}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","authors":[{"uuid":"42154fe0-619c-427a-9799-1433808f8921","emails":["phintz@berkeley.edu"],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1272295"},"full_name":"Hintz, Peter","affiliations":[{"value":"UC, Berkeley, Math. Dept.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903300"}}],"signature_block":"HADp"},{"uuid":"af8f4413-d13e-49eb-8a92-c04e37789640","emails":["andras@math.stanford.edu"],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1272296"},"full_name":"Vasy, András","affiliations":[{"value":"Stanford U., Math. Dept.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/904207"}}],"signature_block":"VASYa"}],"curated":true,"license":[{"url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","license":"arXiv nonexclusive-distrib 1.0","material":"preprint"},{"url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","imposing":"arXiv"}],"texkeys":["Hintz:2016gwb"],"citeable":true,"imprints":[{"date":"2018"}],"keywords":[{"value":"Einstein’s equation","source":"author"},{"value":"black hole stability","source":"author"},{"value":"constraint damping","source":"author"},{"value":"global iteration","source":"author"},{"value":"gauge modification","source":"author"},{"value":"Nash-Moser iteration","source":"author"},{"value":"Nash–Moser iteration","source":"author"},{"value":"microlocal analysis","source":"author"},{"value":"Kerr-de Sitter family of black holes","source":"author"},{"value":"83C57","source":"author"},{"value":"35B40","source":"author"},{"value":"58J47","source":"author"},{"value":"83C05","source":"author"},{"value":"83C35","source":"author"}],"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"We establish the full global non-linear stability of the Kerr-de Sitter family of black holes, as solutions of the initial value problem for the Einstein vacuum equations with positive cosmological constant, for small angular momenta, and without any symmetry assumptions on the initial data. We achieve this by extending the linear and non-linear analysis on black hole spacetimes described in a sequence of earlier papers by the authors: we develop a general framework which enables us to deal systematically with the diffeomorphism invariance of Einstein’s equations. In particular, the iteration scheme used to solve Einstein’s equations automatically finds the parameters of the Kerr-de Sitter black hole that the solution is asymptotic to, the exponentially decaying tail of the solution, and the gauge in which we are able to find the solution; the gauge here is a wave map/DeTurck type gauge, modified by source terms which are treated as unknowns, lying in a suitable finite-dimensional space.","source":"FIZ Karlsruhe"},{"value":"We establish the full global non-linear stability of the Kerr–de Sitter family of black holes, as solutions of the initial value problem for the Einstein vacuum equations with positive cosmological constant, for small angular momenta, and without any symmetry assumptions on the initial data. We achieve this by extending the linear and non-linear analysis on black hole spacetimes described in a sequence of earlier papers by the authors: we develop a general framework which enables us to deal systematically with the diffeomorphism invariance of Einstein’s equations. In particular, the iteration scheme used to solve Einstein’s equations automatically finds the parameters of the Kerr–de Sitter black hole that the solution is asymptotic to, the exponentially decaying tail of the solution, and the gauge in which we are able to find the solution; the gauge here is a wave map/DeTurck type gauge, modified by source terms which are treated as unknowns, lying in a suitable finite-dimensional space.","source":"International Press"},{"value":"We establish the full global non-linear stability of the Kerr-de Sitter family of black holes, as solutions of the initial value problem for the Einstein vacuum equations with positive cosmological constant, for small angular momenta, and without any symmetry assumptions on the initial data. We achieve this by extending the linear and non-linear analysis on black hole spacetimes described in a sequence of earlier papers by the authors: We develop a general framework which enables us to deal systematically with the diffeomorphism invariance of Einstein's equations. In particular, the iteration scheme used to solve Einstein's equations automatically finds the parameters of the Kerr-de Sitter black hole that the solution is asymptotic to, the exponentially decaying tail of the solution, and the gauge in which we are able to find the solution; the gauge here is a wave map/DeTurck type gauge, modified by source terms which are treated as unknowns, lying in a suitable finite-dimensional space.","source":"arXiv"}],"references":[{"raw_refs":[{"value":"[AB15a] Lars Andersson and Pieter Blue. Hidden symmetries and decay for the wave equation on the Kerr spacetime. Annals of Mathematics, 182:787–853, 2015.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["Lars Andersson and Pieter Blue. Hidden symmetries and decay for the wave equation on the Kerr spacetime"],"label":"AB15a","texkey":"AnderssonBlueHiddenKerr","publication_info":{"year":2015,"page_end":"853","page_start":"787","journal_title":"Annals Math.","journal_volume":"182"}}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1257974"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[AB15b] Lars Andersson and Pieter Blue. Uniform energy bound and asymptotics for the Maxwell field on a slowly rotating Kerr black hole exterior. Journal of Hyperbolic Differential Equations, 12(04):689–743, 2015.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["Lars Andersson and Pieter Blue. Uniform energy bound and asymptotics for the Maxwell field on a slowly rotating Kerr black hole exterior"],"label":"AB15b","texkey":"AnderssonBlueMaxwellKerr","publication_info":{"year":2015,"page_end":"743","page_start":"689","journal_title":"J.Hyperbol.Diff.Equat.","journal_volume":"12"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1226229"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[AIK14] Spyros Alexakis, Alexandru D. Ionescu, and Sergiu Klainerman. Rigidity of stationary black holes with small angular momentum on the horizon. Duke Math. J., 163(14):2603–2615, 2014.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["Spyros Alexakis / and Sergiu Klainerman. Rigidity of stationary black holes with small angular momentum on the horizon"],"label":"AIK14","texkey":"AlexakisIonescuKlainermanUniqueness","authors":[{"full_name":"Ionescu"},{"full_name":"Alexandru"}],"publication_info":{"year":2014,"page_end":"2615","page_start":"2603","journal_title":"Duke Math.J.","journa